, animations, and navigation controls.\n\nI want to extend this application into a beginner-friendly DSA learning platform.\n\nMy goal is to learn Data Structures and Algorithms from the fundamentals, practice curated LeetCode problems, understand solution patterns, visualize Python execution, and track my progress.\n\n2. Non-Negotiable Requirements\n\nDo not rebuild my application from scratch.\n\nDo not replace or rewrite my existing execution engine.\n\nDo not modify the original Python code used by the existing visualizer.\n\nPreserve all existing working features, animations, navigation, and explanations.\n\nDo not introduce OpenAI, Gemini, Claude, or any other AI APIs.\n\nDo not require API keys, paid services, cloud databases, authentication, or mandatory internet access.\n\nUse Python as the only supported programming language initially.\n\nStore learning progress locally on my computer.\n\nReuse existing components, dependencies, and architecture wherever possible.\n\nInspect the project before making changes.\n\nMake incremental changes and test them before proceeding.\n\n3. Phase 1: Create the DSA Learning Dashboard\n\nAdd a new navigation section called \"DSA Learning\".\n\nBuild a clean, beginner-friendly dashboard that matches the existing application's design.\n\nInclude:\n\nTotal problems in the curated library.\n\nProblems solved.\n\nProblems attempted.\n\nProblems not started.\n\nBookmarked problems.\n\nTopic-wise progress.\n\nDifficulty-wise progress.\n\nContinue Learning.\n\nRecently practiced problems.\n\nA beginner learning roadmap.\n\nUse actual saved data for progress statistics. Do not generate fake completion numbers or streaks.\n\nInitially include 300 curated, distinct DSA problems. These must be real, identifiable problems, not 300 generated titles or duplicated entries.\n\n\n<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **Core Request**: Extend the existing \"Teach Me This Code\" application (`C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\code-flow-visualizer\\app_build\\`) into a beginner-friendly DSA learning platform without rebuilding from scratch or touching the core engine.\n   - **Phase 1 Deliverables**:\n     1. Add a new navigation section called \"DSA Learning\" (seamless top-level switcher between \"Code Visualizer\" and \"DSA Learning\").\n     2. Build a clean, beginner-friendly DSA Learning Dashboard that matches existing styling.\n     3. Track and display: Total problems (300), Problems solved, Problems attempted, Problems not started, Bookmarked problems.\n     4. Topic-wise progress across all core DSA topics (clickable filters).\n     5. Difficulty-wise progress (Easy, Medium, Hard breakdown).\n     6. \"Continue Learning\" card (linking directly to next recommended or recently touched problem).\n     7. Recently practiced problems list (with timestamp, difficulty, topic, status, and direct \"Solve & Visualize\" action).\n     8. A beginner learning roadmap (8 structured phases).\n     9. 100% real saved progress data stored locally (`localStorage`), zero fake completion numbers or fake streaks.\n     10. Include initially 300 curated, distinct, identifiable DSA problems (real LeetCode numbers, real titles, patterns, descriptions, and runnable Python solutions).\n   - **Scope Boundaries**:\n     - Do NOT rebuild from scratch.\n     - Do NOT modify or rewrite the execution engine (`engine.js`).\n     - Do NOT modify the original Python code used by existing visualizer (Kadane max subarray output 6 must remain verified).\n     - Preserve all existing working features, animations, navigation, explanations, and prediction quizzes.\n     - 100% offline client-side vanilla JavaScript/CSS (Zero AI APIs like OpenAI/Gemini/Claude, no paid services, no cloud databases, no mandatory internet).\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed**:\n     - Inspected `code-flow-visualizer/app_build/` directory (`index.html`, `styles.css`, `app.js`, `engine.js`, `explainer.js`).\n     - Created `scratch/generate_a